<title>NORWAY: Aker RGI shipyard wins 300 mln NOK deal.</title>
<headline>Aker RGI shipyard wins 300 mln NOK deal.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian industrial group Aker RGI ASA said on Friday its Brattvaag Skipsverft AS shipyard had signed contracts for delivery of two supply ships worth a total of 300 million crowns.  </p>
<p>The contracts were signed with Norway's Olympic Shipping AS and with Sanko Steamship CO Ltd of Japan for delivery in March 1999 and December 1998 respectively, a statement said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
